{"path":"api/environment_variables.html","title":"Environment Variables","description":"Environment variables are variables associated to the environment the Node.js process runs in.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_environment_variables"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment-variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment variables are variables associated to the environment the Node.js process runs in."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"CLI Environment Variables"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_cli_environment_variables"},{"type":"anchor","id":"cli-environment-variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There is a set of environment variables that can be defined to customize the behavior of Node.js, for more details refer to the "},{"type":"link","href":"api/cli.html#environment-variables_1","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"CLI Environment Variables documentation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"process.env"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_process_env"},{"type":"anchor","id":"processenv"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The basic API for interacting with environment variables is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"process.env"},{"type":"text","value":", it consists of an object with pre-populated user environment variables that can be modified and expanded."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For more details refer to the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://nodejs.org/api/process.html#processenv","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"process.env"},{"type":"text","value":" documentation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"DotEnv"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_dotenv"},{"type":"anchor","id":"dotenv"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"api/documentation.html#stability-index","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stability: 2"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Stable"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set of utilities for dealing with additional environment variables defined in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" files."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":".env files"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_env_files"},{"type":"anchor","id":"env-files"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" files (also known as dotenv files) are files that define environment variables, which Node.js applications can then interact with (popularized by the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/motdotla/dotenv","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"dotenv"}]},{"type":"text","value":" package)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following is an example of the content of a basic "},{"type":"inline_code","code":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" file:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"text","code":"MY_VAR_A = \"my variable A\"\nMY_VAR_B = \"my variable B\""},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This type of file is used in various different programming languages and platforms but there is no formal specification for it, therefore Node.js defines its own specification described below."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inline_code","code":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" file is a file that contains key-value pairs, each pair is represented by a variable name followed by the equal sign ("},{"type":"inline_code","code":"="},{"type":"text","value":") followed by a variable value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The name of such files is usually "},{"type":"inline_code","code":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" or it starts with "},{"type":"inline_code","code":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" (like for example "},{"type":"inline_code","code":".env.dev"},{"type":"text","value":" where "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"dev"},{"type":"text","value":" indicates a specific target environment). This is the recommended naming scheme but it is not mandatory and dotenv files can have any arbitrary file name."}]},{"type":"heading","level":4,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Variable Names"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_variable_names"},{"type":"anchor","id":"variable-names"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A valid variable name must contain only letters (uppercase or lowercase), digits and underscores ("},{"type":"inline_code","code":"_"},{"type":"text","value":") and it can't begin with a digit."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"More specifically a valid variable name must match the following regular expression:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"text","code":"^[a-zA-Z_]+[a-zA-Z0-9_]*$"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The recommended convention is to use capital letters with underscores and digits when necessary, but any variable name respecting the above definition will work just fine."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, the following are some valid variable names: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"MY_VAR"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"MY_VAR_1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"my_var"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"my_var_1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"myVar"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"My_Var123"},{"type":"text","value":", while these are instead not valid: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"1_VAR"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'my-var'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"\"my var\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"VAR_#1"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":4,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Variable Values"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_variable_values"},{"type":"anchor","id":"variable-values"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Variable values are comprised by any arbitrary text, which can optionally be wrapped inside single ("},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'"},{"type":"text","value":") or double ("},{"type":"inline_code","code":"\""},{"type":"text","value":") quotes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quoted variables can span across multiple lines, while non quoted ones are restricted to a single line."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Noting that when parsed by Node.js all values are interpreted as text, meaning that any value will result in a JavaScript string inside Node.js. For example the following values: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"0"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"{ \"hello\": \"world\" }"},{"type":"text","value":" will result in the literal strings "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'0'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'true'"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'{ \"hello\": \"world\" }'"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of the number zero, the boolean "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" and an object with the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"hello"},{"type":"text","value":" property respectively."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of valid variables:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"text","code":"MY_SIMPLE_VAR = a simple single line variable\nMY_EQUALS_VAR = \"this variable contains an = sign!\"\nMY_HASH_VAR = 'this variable contains a # symbol!'\nMY_MULTILINE_VAR = '\nthis is a multiline variable containing\ntwo separate lines\\nSorry, I meant three lines'"},{"type":"heading","level":4,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spacing"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_spacing"},{"type":"anchor","id":"spacing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Leading and trailing whitespace characters around variable keys and values are ignored unless they are enclosed within quotes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"text","code":"   MY_VAR_A   =    my variable a\n    MY_VAR_B   =    '   my variable b   '"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"will be treated identically to:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"text","code":"MY_VAR_A = my variable a\nMY_VAR_B = '   my variable b   '"},{"type":"heading","level":4,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comments"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_comments"},{"type":"anchor","id":"comments"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hash-tag ("},{"type":"inline_code","code":"#"},{"type":"text","value":") characters denote the beginning of a comment, meaning that the rest of the line will be completely ignored."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hash-tags found within quotes are however treated as any other standard character."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"text","code":"# This is a comment\nMY_VAR = my variable # This is also a comment\nMY_VAR_A = \"# this is NOT a comment\""},{"type":"heading","level":4,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"export"},{"type":"text","value":" prefixes"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_export_prefixes"},{"type":"anchor","id":"export-prefixes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"export"},{"type":"text","value":" keyword can optionally be added in front of variable declarations, such keyword will be completely ignored by all processing done on the file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is useful so that the file can be sourced, without modifications, in shell terminals."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"text","code":"export MY_VAR = my variable"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"CLI Options"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_cli_options"},{"type":"anchor","id":"cli-options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" files can be used to populate the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"process.env"},{"type":"text","value":" object via one the following CLI options:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"api/cli.html#--env-filefile","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"--env-file=file"}]}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"api/cli.html#--env-file-if-existsfile","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"--env-file-if-exists=file"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Programmatic APIs"},{"type":"anchor","id":"environment_variables_programmatic_apis"},{"type":"anchor","id":"programmatic-apis"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There following two functions allow you to directly interact with "},{"type":"inline_code","code":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" files:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://nodejs.org/api/process.html#processloadenvfilepath","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"process.loadEnvFile"}]},{"type":"text","value":" loads an "},{"type":"inline_code","code":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" file and populates "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"process.env"},{"type":"text","value":" with its variables"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://nodejs.org/api/util.html#utilparseenvcontent","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"util.parseEnv"}]},{"type":"text","value":" parses the raw content of an "},{"type":"inline_code","code":".env"},{"type":"text","value":" file and returns its value in an object"}]}]}]}]}}
